  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「オガサワラスズメノヒエ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AA%E3%82%AC%E3%82%B5%E3%83%AF%E3%83%A9%E3%82%B9%E3%82%BA%E3%83%A1%E3%83%8E%E3%83%92%E3%82%A8",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106351836,
      "text": "オガサワラスズメノヒエ Paspalum conjugatum は、イネ科の植物で、熱帯性の小柄な雑草。細長い柄の先端から、小さな小穂の密生する軸を2本、T字型に生じる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Paspalum conjugatum」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paspalum_conjugatum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1309277980,
      "text": "Paspalum conjugatum, commonly known as carabao grass or hilo grass, is a tropical to subtropical perennial grass. It is originally from the American tropics, but has been naturalized widely in tropical Southeast Asia and Pacific Islands. It has also spread to Northern Africa and Northern Eastern Australia, and New Zealand. It is also known as sour paspalum, T-grass, or more confusingly, as \"buffalo grass\" or \"sour grass\"."
    }
